# Lab 12 – Ethics, Fairness, and Bias

## Overview
This lab explored fairness and bias in machine learning models.

## What I Learned
- How model performance can differ across groups
- How to compare subgroup accuracy
- How false positive and false negative rates can show unfair outcomes
- Why removing a sensitive column does not always remove bias

## Tools Used
- Python
- pandas
- scikit-learn

## Reflection
This lab helped me understand that machine learning models can affect people differently and should be reviewed carefully before being used in real-world decisions.
